---
import AccountGroups from "./nova/xf/AccountGroups.astro";
import PolicyDelivery from "./nova/xf/PolicyDelivery.astro";
import NameLookup from "./nova/xf/NameLookup.astro";
import Files01DocumentImages from "./Files01DocumentImages.astro";

import {linksForSystem} from "../data/policies";
import EvidencePanel from "./EvidencePanel.astro";
interface Props {secondary?:boolean}
const {secondary=false}=Astro.props;
const name=secondary?"NOVA-DC02":"NOVA-DC01", partner=secondary?"NOVA-DC01":"NOVA-DC02", vm=secondary?"102":"101";
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const inside=[
["Active Directory","Company accounts, computers, groups and organizational units","learn/active-directory/"],
["Company directory","Explore the actual users, groups and OUs","directory/"],
["DNS","Find the address of a computer or domain service","learn/dns/"],
["Kerberos","Authenticate users through tickets","learn/kerberos/"],
["LDAP","Query directory information","learn/ldap/"],
["SYSVOL","Stores shared domain policy files","learn/sysvol/"],["NETLOGON","Makes sign-in scripts available to employees","learn/netlogon/"],
["Group Policy","Manage company computer and user settings","learn/group-policy/"],
["Replication","Keep directory changes in sync with "+partner,"learn/replication/"],
["System State backup","Protect critical directory configuration","learn/system-state/"],["FSMO roles and Windows Time","Special responsibilities held by DC02","systems/nova-dc02/#fsmo-roles"]];
const incidents=[
["Controlled test · Primary domain controller unavailable","DC01 went offline. Sign-ins and the file share kept working through DC02.","dc01-outage"],
["Controlled test · Directory replication interrupted","I blocked replication on purpose. A new group stayed missing on DC02 until I restored it.","replication-divergence"],
["Unexpected · Incorrect subnet prefix","DC01 and DC02 were set to /32 and the new file server to /24, so replies took the wrong road.","fileserver-subnet"],
["Blind test · DNS client outage","A wrong DNS setting on the workstation stopped it opening the share by name.","dns-client-outage"]];
const specs=[["Hostname",name+".nova.corp"],["VM ID",vm],["Hypervisor","NOVA-PROX01"],["CPU","2 vCPU"],["RAM","4 GiB"],["Operating system","Windows Server 2025 Standard"],["IP address",secondary?"10.10.20.11/24":"10.10.20.10/24"],["Network","INFRA / VLAN 20"],["Gateway","10.10.20.1"],["DNS order","10.10.20.11, 10.10.20.10"],["Domain","nova.corp"],["Virtual disks",secondary?"60G OS":"80G OS · 60G attached data disk"],["Firmware / machine","OVMF / q35"],["NIC / bridge","net0 / vmbr1"],["Roles","AD DS, DNS"],["Services","NTDS, DNS, Netlogon"],["Replication partner",partner],["FSMO roles",secondary?"All five roles":"Held by NOVA-DC02"],["Directory","Writable DC"]];
---
<section class="section compact"><div class="container grid-main deep-system-profile dc-profile"><article>
<section class="content-section"><h2>What is {name}?</h2><p>{name} is one of Nova Corp's two Windows Domain Controllers. It stores company accounts, helps employees sign in, and helps computers find company services. Both controllers hold the nova.corp directory and can answer authentication and DNS requests.</p><p>{secondary?"I added this second controller so sign-in keeps working when DC01 is offline. It also holds the five FSMO roles.":"This is the first domain controller. DC02 holds a second writable copy of the directory."}</p><EvidencePanel subject={name+" server overview"} requested={"A reviewed Server Manager or Proxmox hardware screenshot of "+name+" is needed."}/></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>Why does Nova Corp need it and what problems does it solve?</h2>
<div class="pilot-story"><h3>1. Managing employee accounts in one place</h3><h4 class="story-label problem-label">Problem</h4><p>Imagine <a href={base+"people/moyo/"}>Moyo</a> joins IT. Without a domain controller I would create a separate account on every computer she uses, and update each one if she moves or leaves.</p><h4 class="story-label solution-label">Solution</h4><p>I built the Active Directory domain nova.corp. I create Moyo's account once, put it in the IT organizational unit and add her to IT_Users. Every domain-joined computer checks the directory to identify her, and a change is made in one place.</p><AccountGroups /><EvidencePanel subject="Active Directory Users and Computers" requested="A reviewed directory screenshot showing the IT OU and its accounts is needed."/></div>
<div class="pilot-story"><h3>2. Applying company rules consistently</h3><h4 class="story-label problem-label">Problem</h4><p>Every new workstation needs the same firewall settings and security rules as the others. Setting each one by hand risks missing something.</p><h4 class="story-label solution-label">Solution</h4><p>Nova Corp uses <a href={base+"learn/group-policy/"}>Group Policy</a> to set user and computer settings centrally. The workstation baseline turns on Windows Firewall and disables SMBv1. Contractor accounts get a separate removable-storage rule. Each computer fetches its policies from the domain.</p><PolicyDelivery /><figure class="dc-photo"><img src={base+"evidence/05-firewall-gpo-configuration.png"} alt="Windows Firewall Group Policy configuration"/><figcaption><strong>Workstation security policy</strong><p>Windows Firewall settings configured in Group Policy.</p></figcaption></figure><p><a href={base+"policies/"}>Explore Nova Corp's policies →</a></p></div>
<div class="pilot-story"><h3>3. Verifying identities and controlling access</h3><h4 class="story-label problem-label">Problem</h4><p>Moyo must open the IT folder but never the Finance files. The file server needs a trustworthy way to know who she is.</p><h4 class="story-label solution-label">Solution</h4><p>The domain controller signs Moyo in with <a href={base+"learn/kerberos/"}>Kerberos</a>. Her groups decide what she may open, and NOVA-FILES01 then checks its own share and folder permissions. My workstation test showed IT access allowed and Finance denied.</p><Files01DocumentImages ids={["fileserver-client-baseline"]}/></div>
<div class="pilot-story"><h3>4. Finding servers by name</h3><h4 class="story-label problem-label">Problem</h4><p>An employee opens the file server by name. Nobody should have to remember an IP address, and Windows also has to find a domain controller to sign in.</p><h4 class="story-label solution-label">Solution</h4><p>Nova Corp runs <a href={base+"learn/dns/"}>DNS</a> on both domain controllers. The workstation resolves NOVA-FILES01 to 10.10.20.20 and uses service records to find the domain services it needs.</p><NameLookup /><Files01DocumentImages ids={["dns-timeout"]}/><p>This screenshot is from a separate DNS failure I caused on purpose.</p></div>
<div class="pilot-story"><h3>5. Supporting growth and keeping sign-in available</h3><h4 class="story-label problem-label">Problem</h4><p>With only one directory server, everything depends on it. If it goes offline, employees could not find domain services or get fresh sign-in tickets.</p><h4 class="story-label solution-label">Solution</h4><p>Nova Corp has two writable domain controllers that copy changes to each other. When I switched DC01 off on purpose, Moyo still signed in, got fresh tickets through DC02 and opened the IT share. After DC01 came back, replication caught up.</p><Files01DocumentImages ids={["dc02-sysvol-available","dc01-recovery-gpupdate"]}/><p><a href={base+"learn/replication/"}>How directory replication works →</a></p></div>
</section>
{secondary&&<section id="fsmo-roles" class="content-section"><h2>Additional responsibilities of NOVA-DC02</h2><p>DC02 holds all five FSMO roles. These are special directory responsibilities, not five separate Windows services. Both controllers provide Kerberos, DNS and directory services.</p><div class="card-list">{[["Schema Master","Controls changes to the directory schema."],["Domain Naming Master","Controls additions and removals of domains in the forest."],["RID Master","Allocates pools of identifiers used when creating security principals."],["PDC Emulator","Supports password-change coordination and anchors the domain time hierarchy."],["Infrastructure Master","Maintains cross-domain object references."]].map(([title,body])=><details class="system-card"><summary>{title}</summary><p>{body}</p><p><strong>Verify ownership on a DC:</strong></p><pre><code>netdom query fsmo</code></pre><p>Expected: {title} points to NOVA-DC02.</p></details>)}</div><p>DC02 follows an external NTP source; DC01 follows the domain time hierarchy. Kerberos depends on accurate clocks. <strong>Check on each controller:</strong> <code>w32tm /query /source</code>; DC02 should use its configured external source, while DC01 follows the domain hierarchy. <a href={base+"learn/kerberos/"}>Kerberos →</a> · <a href={base+"learn/replication/"}>Replication →</a></p></section>}
<section class="content-section"><h2>Inside this server</h2><div class="card-list">{inside.map(([name,description,route])=><a class="system-card" href={base+route}><h3>{name}</h3><p>{description}</p><span class="readmore">Explore →</span></a>)}</div></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>How {name} connects to Nova Corp</h2></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>Related tests and incidents</h2><div class="card-list">{incidents.map(([title,description,slug])=><a class="system-card" href={base+"incidents/"+slug+"/"}><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p><span class="readmore">Read investigation →</span></a>)}</div><h3>Other recorded validation</h3><p>Directory health, LDAP and Kerberos service discovery, SYSVOL and NETLOGON, and Active Directory Recycle Bin recovery were tested. DC01 has a daily System State backup at 23:00; a complete System State restoration has not been demonstrated. DC02 has no recorded Proxmox archive in the published inventory. The saved DC policy sets LDAP signing to None; effective LDAP signing needs a separate security check.</p><details><summary>Technical checks</summary><p>Run these read-only diagnostics on the controller. Expected results are what a healthy system returns.</p>{[["Core services","Get-Service NTDS,DNS,DFSR,Netlogon,Kdc,W32Time","The listed services should be Running."],["Directory health","dcdiag /test:Advertising /test:SysVolCheck /test:NetLogons","Each selected test should pass."],["Replication","repadmin /replsummary","Zero replication failures."],["Replication partner","repadmin /showrepl "+name,"Each naming context should report a successful last attempt."],["DNS discovery",'Resolve-DnsName -Type SRV "_ldap._tcp.dc._msdcs.nova.corp"',"The domain controller service records should resolve."],["FSMO ownership","netdom query fsmo","All five roles should point to NOVA-DC02."],["Time synchronization","w32tm /query /source","DC02 should use its configured external source; DC01 should follow domain hierarchy."],["Kerberos","klist","In an authenticated user session, appropriate valid tickets should be present."]].map(([title,command,expected])=><div class="health-check"><h3>{title}</h3><p><strong>Where:</strong> {title==="Kerberos"?"Authenticated domain user session":name+" or authorized management PC with the relevant tools"}</p><pre><code>{command}</code></pre><p><strong>Expected:</strong> {expected}</p></div>)}</details></section>
<section class="content-section"><details><summary>Related to this server</summary><p><a href={base+"computers/"+name.toLowerCase()+"/"}>AD computer object</a> · <a href={base+"directory/ous/domain-controllers/"}>Domain Controllers OU</a></p>{linksForSystem(name.toLowerCase()).map(p=><p><a href={base+"policies/"+p.slug+"/"}>{p.name}</a></p>)}</details></section>
<section class="content-section"><h2>Engineering journals</h2>{[["CR-003 · Install Active Directory and DNS","Journal-CR-003"],["CR-004 · Additional domain controller","Journal-CR-004"],["CR-005 · Directory accounts and groups","Journal-CR-005"],["CR-013 · Directory resilience","CR-013_Secondary_Domain_Controller_and_AD_Resilience_Journal"]].map(([title,slug])=><p><a href={base+"reference/Documentation/Change-Requests/"+slug+"/"}>{title} →</a></p>)}<p><a href={base+"pdf-journals/Nova_Corp_CR-014_Engineering_Journal_and_Evidence.pdf"}>CR-014 · Controlled incident exercises →</a></p><p><a href={base+"reference/explore/systems/"+name+"/"}>Original system reference →</a></p><p><a href={base+"reference/explore/virtualization/vms/"+vm+"/"}>Exact VM configuration →</a></p></section>
</article><aside><div class="sidebox"><h3>Technical Profile</h3><dl class="fact-list">{specs.map(([label,value])=><div><dt>{label}</dt><dd>{value}</dd></div>)}</dl></div></aside></div></section>
<style>.dc-profile>*{min-width:0}.dc-profile .content-section{margin-bottom:45px}.dc-profile p{line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 14px}.dc-profile h3{margin:20px 0 10px}.dc-profile pre{overflow:auto;max-width:100%}.dc-diagram{margin:20px 0;padding:20px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:10px;text-align:center}.dc-node{padding:14px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:8px;display:grid;gap:6px;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.dc-node small,.dc-arrow small{display:block;color:var(--ink);font-size:.8rem}.dc-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto minmax(0,1fr);gap:10px;align-items:center}.dc-arrow{padding:12px 0;color:var(--c-amber);font-size:.8rem}.dc-diagram figcaption{font-size:.82rem;margin-top:16px;color:var(--ink)}.dc-profile aside{position:sticky;top:100px;max-height:calc(100vh - 120px);overflow:auto}@media(max-width:1000px){.dc-profile aside{position:static;max-height:none}}.pilot-story{border-top:1px solid var(--line,rgba(150,150,150,.25));padding:24px 0}.story-label{font-size:1rem;letter-spacing:.02em;margin:25px 0 6px}.problem-label{color:var(--c-red)}.solution-label{color:var(--c-green)}.dc-photo{margin:26px 0 32px}.dc-photo img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.dc-photo figcaption{text-align:center;font-size:.84rem}.dc-arrow{position:relative}.dc-arrow:after{content:"";display:block;width:60%;height:2px;margin:8px auto 0;background:repeating-linear-gradient(90deg,#bba987 0 8px,transparent 8px 16px);background-size:32px 2px;animation:dcflow 1.8s linear infinite}@keyframes dcflow{to{background-position:32px 0}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.dc-arrow:after{animation:none}}.health-check{margin:20px 0}.health-check pre{overflow:auto;max-width:100%}</style>
